==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-alimony.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Etymology===
Known since 1655, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|lang=la|alimonia||food, support, nourishment, sustenance}}, itself from {{term|lang=la|alere||to nourish}} + {{term|lang=la|-monia||action, state, condition}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|alimonies}}

# {{legal}} A [[court]]-[[enforce]]d [[allowance]] made to a former [[spouse]] by a [[divorce]]d or [[legally]] [[separated]] person.
# The [[means]] to [[support]] [[life]].

